  "content": "## People, households and groups\n\nCCB v2 addresses records by integer ids. Resolve a person from the individual\nlist and a household from families; never guess ids. Family membership and\nchurch group membership join by individual id. A membership role belongs to\nthat group, rather than being a property of the person everywhere.\n\nIdentity Auth acts with the signed-in person's permissions. A permission\nrefusal can mean that person lacks access even when the connection is healthy.\n\n## Events and attendance\n\nAn event is a series; its dated occurrence is a separate identity. Attendance\njoins need both the event id and occurrence. Preserve the vendor's date and\ntime-zone meaning instead of treating every occurrence as UTC midnight.\n\n## Pastoral and financial records\n\nNotes, background checks, pledges and giving metrics can be sensitive. Read\nonly what the task needs and reduce those records inside execute_code before\nreturning an answer. Gift metrics are counts by period, with a range of at\nmost twelve months. Per-gift transactions and amounts belong to the legacy\nv1 XML API, which this v2 connector does not reach.\n\n## Vendor call rates and recovery\n\nCCB meters endpoints separately per API client. Individual profile reads have\nno burst; individual advanced searches allow one call per five seconds, and\ncategory schedule lists allow one per two seconds. Prefer list pages over a\nloop of individual gets. Other deployments sharing the client spend from the\nsame vendor allowance.\n\nFor a profile edit, resolve the individual first and preserve fields outside\nthe requested change. Use `ccb_api_write` for the edit; the host may ask the\nuser to confirm. After an ambiguous update, read that profile to determine\nwhat actually changed before deciding whether another write is needed.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Paging:** a paged `list_*` or `search_*` read takes `limit` (default 25, at most 100) and `cursor`. While `page.hasMore` is true, pass `page.nextCursor` back unchanged as `cursor`; the last page has no `nextCursor`.\n- **Paging:** on a paged hatch read, keep the original method, path, filters, limit and fields. Pass `page.nextCursor` unchanged as the top-level `cursor`; omit raw anchors on continuations. The last page has `page.hasMore: false` and no `nextCursor`. If `page.hasMore` is true without a cursor, the data is incomplete and continuation could not be confined.\n- **Results:** `fields` narrows a read's result to the dot paths you name. `truncated` lists the dot paths a result cut for size; the ids that fetch what was cut stay in the result.\n- **Hatch:** `ccb_api_search` finds this API's operations and reads no account data, `ccb_api_details` shows one operation's contract, and `ccb_api_read` calls a reviewed read. `ccb_api_write` calls a reviewed write; the host may ask the user to confirm it. An operation without a reviewed verdict is refused; these are refused by design: `POST /data_import/individuals`, `POST /data_import/sacraments`, `POST /events/{id}/photo`, `POST /families/{id}/photo`, `POST /files`, `POST /groups/{id}/photo`, `POST /individuals/{id}/files/{file_id}`, `POST /individuals/{id}/files`, `POST /individuals/{id}/photo`, `POST /oauth/token`, `POST /reset_password`, `POST /scheduling/categories/{id}/files`, `POST /scheduling/categories/{id}/messages`, `POST /scheduling/events/{id}/files`.\n- **Writes:** a write is sent once and never retried. When its outcome is unknown, read the target before repeating it. Writes take no idempotency key.\n- **Errors:** codes come from the vendor's statuses and error facts, never its prose. `not_found` means the record does not exist; this API tells absence from a permission gap. It documents no conflict.\n- **Withheld values:** a value withheld for safety reads `\"[redacted]\"`. Writes refuse whole marker values and withheld links; longer prose may mention the marker. Paths and queries refuse any containment.",
